<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">William B. Ide</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1796">1796</a>–<a href="/years/1852">1852</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as William Brown Ide</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">William B. Ide was an American settler in Mexican <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/california">California</a> who was chosen leader of the Bear Flag revolt in June 1846 and proclaimed the California Republic at Sonoma. His command ended when <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/john-c-fremont">John C. Frémont</a> took over the rebel forces in July. He later held local offices in the new state of California.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/william-b-ide.jpg" alt="William B. Ide" width="320" height="382" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:William_Ide.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
